[00:20.38]1. Jehovah God, I call to you and ask you:
[00:25.98]“Hear my prayer.”
[00:28.66]My wounds are deep and slow to heal;
[00:32.20]my load is hard to bear.
[00:37.20]Despondent thoughts and disappointed hopes
[00:41.50]have left me weak.
[00:45.26]O God of comfort, care for me;
[00:49.14]your favor I do seek.
[00:54.36](Chorus)
[00:55.02]Do raise me up; help me endure.
[01:02.84]When I’m in doubt, make my hope sure.
[01:12.30]From deep despair, I turn to you.
[01:21.30]Jehovah God, my strength renew.
[01:40.12]2. Your Word has been my comfort and
[01:44.42]a refuge when I’m weak,
[01:48.86]Expressing feelings dear to me
[01:52.00]in words I cannot speak.
[01:56.66]Please build in me the faith and trust
[02:00.22]that your Word does impart.
[02:04.66]And help me always know your love
[02:09.40]is greater than my heart.
[02:14.66](Chorus)
[02:14.66]Do raise me up; help me endure.
[02:22.84]When I’m in doubt, make my hope sure.
[02:31.36]From deep despair, I turn to you.
[02:41.28]Jehovah God, my strength renew.
